      "problem": "Evaluate $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{100}{98}).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{100}{98})$ means the same thing as ${}_{100}{C}_{98}.$\n\n In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=100$ and $r=98,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{100}{C}_{98} & =\\frac{100!}{(100-98)!\\,98!} \\\\  & =\\frac{100!}{2!\\,98!} \\\\  & =\\frac{100\\cdot 99\\cdot \\cancel{98!}}{2\\,\\cancel{98!}} \\\\  & =4\\,950.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
